Subject: [PATCH 19/21] OPLOG: operation log -- every web command, its reply,
 and each motor's state changes go to runcfg\logs\oplog_YYYYMMDD.txt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260928: "接下來我要測試motor test功能，你能夠透過操作的LOG來知道我的動作對吧? 跟你反應問題你能夠處理清楚解嗎? 不能清楚
解析的話，要強化LOG和state record功能". Before this, Motor Test's presses and the server's answers were only printed to the VS
Code debug console (no file) and the log.event ring was empty (Motor Test sends none), so a problem report could not be traced.
- WebBridgeServer.cpp: webbridge::g_W906OpLogHook (0 = off: tests and every other user unchanged), called for every cmd frame
  as received (RECV, socket thread), every SendAck (ACK: control.*, refusals, malformed), and every CompleteCommand (DONE, tick
  thread). Occupies blank lines / same lines, no line moves.
- tools/wb_serve.cpp (end of file): W906_OpLogInit / W906_OpHook / W906_OpLogMotorRuntime. On only when W906_OPLOG_DIR is set
  (both IOWEB F5 configurations in .vscode/launch.json set it to runcfg\logs). Lines: START (pid, port, token-enforce, exe
  build time), CMD (c<conn>#<id> + raw JSON, 600 bytes max), OK/NG (reply or refusal, 400 bytes max, ms; "socket" for the
  socket-thread answers), MOT (per axis, only the fields that changed old->new, plus cmd/enc position; first one = baseline;
  fields svo alm st busy homing homeJob loopJob homeFlag cw home ccw emg ledAlm softCw softCcw q err, taken from the same
  /api/struct/motor/runtime body the page reads, after every W906_ApiCacheRefresh), PAGE (Motor Test lock / lock text, motor
  power relay / state / pending, selected motor, Light Scale). fflush per line (readable while running), one file per day.
  Quiet unless they fail: sys.ping, ui.windows.put, cfg.resync, *.get, control.acquire, control.release (first run 20260929:
  acquire/release were 422 of 1178 lines in 4 minutes). auth.* / security.* / any frame mentioning passw / pwd / pwbook: the
  command content and the reply are NOT written, only the name, ok/ng and executed/guard.
- cStateRecord.cpp (NOT golden, one line on a blank line): a State Record also copies today's oplog into its folder (background
  job, before the zip); nothing when W906_OPLOG_DIR is not set.
Verified: the first run (EastSun's F5 20260929 09:32) wrote 1178 lines: START, MOT baselines, the motor power relay going on,
MInArmX / MInArmY selected, "*Lock by [00] MInArmX moveing" / "*Lock by Homeing", IO outputs refused with the engine's reason.
Build build_integ_ship_x86 --target wb_serve exit 0, no warning in the new code; pe_truncation_check 178 complete.

